# All of these are optional. For local testing (`npx wrangler dev`), copy
# what you need to `.dev.vars` (gitignored). For a real deployment, set them
# with `npx wrangler secret put <NAME>` (or the Deploy button's prompts) —
# never commit real values.

# Room audio (LiveKit). Leave all three unset to keep room audio off
# (POST /rooms/{id}/audio 404s — same as tinker-server without --livekit-*).
# Create a project at https://cloud.livekit.io, then Settings -> Keys.
# LIVEKIT_URL=wss://<project>.livekit.cloud
# LIVEKIT_KEY=<api key>
# LIVEKIT_SECRET=<api secret>

# GitHub sign-in. Create a GitHub OAuth app (Settings -> Developer settings
# -> OAuth Apps; any homepage/callback URL; tick "Enable Device Flow") and
# set its client id. Leave unset to disable GitHub sign-in — guest sign-in
# works either way, with no setup.
# GITHUB_CLIENT_ID=Iv1.abc123

# There is no DEV_AUTH here on purpose. This bundle is what a real deploy
# runs, and dev sign-in (anyone can sign in as anyone) must never be
# reachable on a public Worker — it only exists for `wrangler dev` in the
# main Tinker repo's own hosts/cloudflare checkout, never in a deployed
# environment's vars or secrets.
